extend type Query {
  """Paginated snapshot of supported logistics entities of one force in a bounded area: transport belts, underground belts, splitters, loaders, linked belts, inserters, pipes, pipe-to-ground, storage tanks, boilers, pumps and offshore pumps. surface and force must be non-empty and exist; area sides must be positive and at most 256 tiles. type, when non-empty, must be one of those entity types and narrows the page to that type, while pageInfo.total stays the matching count before pagination (limit 1 through 1000, default 100, offset zero-based). Belt-like entities carry lanes with engine transport-line names, sides and contents; inserters carry pickup/drop positions and the held stack; every entity carries engine status, fluid boxes and fuel/output inventories where they exist. Entries are sorted by type, prototype name, position and unit number, and pageInfo.hasMore reports further pages; all entities in a page are read at one tick."""
  worldLogistics(input: WorldLogisticsInput!): WorldLogisticsPage!
  """Paginated snapshot of resource entities, obstacles and pumpable water tiles in a bounded area of one force, with nearby selected-force mining drills. surface and force must be non-empty and exist; area sides must be positive and at most 256 tiles. resourceName filters resource entities only (never obstacles or water); kinds, when non-empty, keeps only the listed entry kinds (resource, tree, cliff, simple-entity, water) and narrows pageInfo.total, while resourceTotal, obstacleTotal and waterTotal remain whole-area counts independent of the kinds filter. Water counts only tiles that collide with water_tile and expose a pumpable fluid, so out-of-map tiles are excluded. drillRadius (0 to 100 tiles, default 10) finds drills by distance from each resource entry; groupPatches instead clusters matching resource entities into adjacency-connected patches sorted by total amount descending, and a patch's nearbyDrills come from its bounds expanded by drillRadius, with patches returned in full and not paginated. Nearby drills are distance matches, not proof of mining coverage; limit (1 through 1000, default 100) and zero-based offset paginate the sorted entries."""
  worldResources(input: WorldResourcesInput!): WorldResourcesPage!
  """Ask the engine's surface.can_place_entity whether one entity prototype of the selected force fits at a position and direction. surface, force and prototype must be non-empty and exist; position must be finite and direction is an engine direction code from 0 to 15. This is an engine collision/build check only: player reach, inventory and researched technology are not considered. When the tile is refused, blockers lists the colliding prototype names found on that tile (deduplicated and sorted), and terrain is true when the ground tile's own collision mask shares a layer with the prototype; both are empty and false when canPlace is true. tile is the ground tile name in either case."""
  worldPlacement(input: WorldPlacementInput!): WorldPlacementResult!
  """Sample engine placement legality for one entity prototype on every tile center of a bounded area and return it only in the shape selected by mode, answering a routing or build-site question in one RCON call instead of one worldPlacement per tile. surface, force and prototype must be non-empty and exist; direction is a direction code from 0 to 15; area sides must be positive and at most 256 tiles, and the sampled tile count may not exceed 16384. All engine checks run in every mode: blockedTiles is filled only in BLOCKED_TILES (the default) and is empty otherwise, rows only in GRID (one string per tile row, top row first, one character per tile, 1 placeable and 0 blocked), and sites only in SITES (greedy largest-first, non-overlapping rectangles of at least siteWidth by siteHeight tiles with the origin at the top-left tile corner; siteWidth/siteHeight must not exceed the area and maxSites is 1 through 200). sampled, placeable and blocked are always filled. Like worldPlacement, this is a surface.can_place_entity check, so player reach, inventory and research are not considered."""
  probePlacement(input: PlacementProbeInput!): PlacementProbeResult!
}

"""Area coordinates must be finite; positive dimensions must each be at most 256 tiles. Limit is 1 through 1000; offset is zero-based and non-negative. Type, if non-empty, must be a supported logistics entity type."""
input WorldLogisticsInput { surface: String! = "nauvis" force: String! = "player" area: FactoryAreaInput! type: String limit: Int! = 100 offset: Int! = 0 }
"""Area has the same bounds and pagination constraints as WorldLogisticsInput. Drill radius is finite and between 0 and 100 tiles. Resource name filters resources only, not obstacles or water. Kinds, when non-empty, keeps only the listed entry kinds (resource, tree, cliff, simple-entity, water) and narrows total; the resource, obstacle and water partition totals stay unfiltered counts for the whole area. GroupPatches clusters matching resource entities into connected patches regardless of the kinds filter."""
input WorldResourcesInput { surface: String! = "nauvis" force: String! = "player" area: FactoryAreaInput! resourceName: String drillRadius: Float! = 10 kinds: [String!] groupPatches: Boolean! = false limit: Int! = 100 offset: Int! = 0 }
"""Surface, force and prototype must be non-empty and exist; coordinates must be finite and direction must be between 0 and 15."""
input WorldPlacementInput { surface: String! = "nauvis" force: String! = "player" prototype: String! position: PositionInput! direction: Int! = 0 }
"""Selects which result list a placement probe fills. BLOCKED_TILES reports every refused tile with its blockers. GRID reports a compact row-major placeability map. SITES reports the largest non-overlapping empty tile rectangles that are at least siteWidth by siteHeight, largest first."""
enum PlacementProbeMode { BLOCKED_TILES GRID SITES }
"""Surface, force and prototype must be non-empty and exist; direction must be between 0 and 15. Area bounds match WorldResourcesInput, but the sampled tile count may not exceed 16384. mode selects which result list is filled (BLOCKED_TILES -> blockedTiles, GRID -> rows, SITES -> sites); siteWidth/siteHeight/maxSites only affect SITES and are tile counts from 1 to the area dimensions, maxSites 1 through 200."""
input PlacementProbeInput { surface: String! = "nauvis" force: String! = "player" prototype: String! direction: Int! = 0 area: FactoryAreaInput! mode: PlacementProbeMode! = BLOCKED_TILES siteWidth: Float! = 1 siteHeight: Float! = 1 maxSites: Int! = 50 }

type WorldArea { leftTopX: Float! leftTopY: Float! rightBottomX: Float! rightBottomY: Float! }
"""One transport line of a belt-like entity. lineName is the engine defines.transport_line name (for example left_line, right_line, secondary_left_line on an underground belt, or a splitter line) and side is left, right, or unknown when the name is unrecognised. Indexes are 1-based and per entity type: 2 for a transport belt, 4 for an underground belt (surface plus tunnel lines), 8 for a splitter."""
type WorldLane { index: Int! lineName: String! side: String! items: [InventoryStack!]! }
"""One-based fluid box index and capacity; name, amount and temperature are null for an empty box."""
type WorldFluid { index: Int! name: String amount: Float temperature: Float capacity: Float! }
type WorldInventory { kind: String! items: [InventoryStack!]! }
type WorldLogisticsEntity { name: String! type: String! position: Position! direction: Int! unitNumber: UnitNumber status: String lanes: [WorldLane!]! heldStack: InventoryStack pickupPosition: Position dropPosition: Position fluids: [WorldFluid!]! worldInventories: [WorldInventory!]! }
"""Inserters whose actual pickup or drop target is the inspected entity, read in a separate game snapshot. Targets fall back to the entity under the arm's geometric pickup/drop position when the engine target is null, so wiring stays visible for inserters that have not run since placement or power loss."""
type InspectionLogistics { tick: Float! inserters: [ConnectedInserter!]! }
"""inserter plus the entities it takes from and drops into. pickup/drop are null only when the arm position touches nothing insertable; a wired inserter reports them even while unpowered or idle."""
type ConnectedInserter { inserter: LogisticsEndpoint! pickup: LogisticsEndpoint drop: LogisticsEndpoint }
"""One inserter, machine, container or belt endpoint. direction is the engine direction code for entities that expose one; lanes carry transport-line names and sides for belt-like entities."""
type LogisticsEndpoint { name: String! type: String! position: Position! unitNumber: UnitNumber status: String direction: Int pickupPosition: Position dropPosition: Position heldStack: InventoryStack lanes: [WorldLane!]! }
"""Total counts matching logistics entities before pagination."""
type WorldLogisticsPage { tick: Float! surface: String! force: String! area: WorldArea! pageInfo: PageInfo! logisticsEntities: [WorldLogisticsEntity!]! }
type WorldDrill { name: String! position: Position! unitNumber: UnitNumber }
"""Resource entities, trees, cliffs, simple entities and water-collision tiles. Nearby drills are distance matches, not proof of mining coverage."""
type WorldResourceEntry { kind: String! name: String! position: Position! amount: Float requiredFluid: String fluidAmount: Float nearbyDrills: [WorldDrill!]! }
"""Totals count matching entries before pagination; resource, obstacle and water totals partition them. Patches are connected resource-entity clusters at least one tile apart from each other, sorted by total amount descending."""
type WorldResourcesPage { tick: Float! surface: String! force: String! area: WorldArea! drillRadius: Float! pageInfo: PageInfo! resourceTotal: Int! obstacleTotal: Int! waterTotal: Int! worldEntries: [WorldResourceEntry!]! patches: [ResourcePatch!]! }
"""One connected resource patch. Bounds and centroid are computed from resource entity positions; nearby drills sit inside the bounds expanded by the request drill radius."""
type ResourcePatch { name: String! tiles: Int! totalAmount: Float! bounds: WorldArea! centroid: Position! nearbyDrills: [WorldDrill!]! }
"""Engine collision/build check only; does not check player reach, inventory or research. When the tile is refused, blockers lists colliding prototype names on that tile, terrain is true when the ground tile itself uses one of the prototype's collision layers, and tile is the ground tile name."""
type WorldPlacementResult { tick: Float! surface: String! force: String! prototype: String! position: Position! direction: Int! canPlace: Boolean! blockers: [String!]! terrain: Boolean! tile: String! }
"""Totals of one placement probe over a tile grid. Result lists are mode-coupled: blockedTiles is filled in BLOCKED_TILES mode (the default) and is empty otherwise; rows is filled only in GRID mode (one string per tile row, top row first, one character per tile, 1 placeable and 0 blocked); sites is filled only in SITES mode (rectangles largest first, origin at the top-left tile corner, never overlapping). sampled/placeable/blocked are always filled."""
type PlacementProbeResult { tick: Float! surface: String! force: String! prototype: String! direction: Int! area: WorldArea! sampled: Int! placeable: Int! blocked: Int! blockedTiles: [PlacementBlockedTile!]! rows: [String!]! sites: [PlacementSite!]! }
"""One empty tile rectangle: width and height in whole tiles starting at the origin tile corner."""
type PlacementSite { origin: Position! width: Float! height: Float! }
"""One refused tile. Blockers are colliding entity prototype names, terrain is true when the tile itself blocks this prototype, and tile is the ground tile prototype name."""
type PlacementBlockedTile { position: Position! blockers: [String!]! terrain: Boolean! tile: String! }
